window.DOCS["6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c"]={"id":"6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c","summary":{"title_zh":"財務機制","what":"這是由第一工作組主席提交的草案，旨在討論如何透過全球環境基金（GEF）及全球生物多樣性綱要基金籌措資金，以落實生物多樣性保護目標。","points":["第 4 段邀請自願承擔已開發締約方義務的締約方與其他國家，為全球環境基金第九次增資提供捐款，以支持綱要的全面落實。","第 8 段歡迎將全球環境基金第九次增資資源的 35% 分配予生物多樣性焦點領域（為最大的焦點領域），並以經濟合作發展組織發展援助委員會的里約標記方法計算，目標在該期間至少 70% 的資金投入生物多樣性。","第 9 段歡迎全球環境基金第九次增資的規劃方向納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，並列入期望性目標：20% 的資源用於支持原住民族與地方社區，對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的期望基準為 35%，以及 25% 的規劃目標用於動員私人資本。","第 12 段請全球環境基金加速強化其成效，包括改善環境公約之間的綜效、透過混合融資窗口促進私部門融資、減少交易成本並簡化取得程序，以及深化原住民族與地方社區取得資金的支持。","第 19 段與第 20 段請全球生物多樣性綱要基金努力動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並邀請已開發締約方、其他政府、私部門及慈善組織作出或增加捐款。","第 33 段通過第十次增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）所需資金完整評估的職權範圍（附件二）；第 38 段請執行秘書委託第七次四年一度財務機制成效檢視報告，並準備前述完整評估的報告。"],"open":["第 1 段與第 2 段：對全球環境基金第九次增資承諾（截至 2026 年 5 月 30 日約 39 億美元，依約定匯率計算，金額待 2026 年 10 月更新）的用語，是「歡迎」、「承認」還是「注意到並讚賞」；第 2 段是否應表示注意到並表示關切，僅有 50% 已開發締約方出資，仍未定案。","第 3 段是否表示深感憂慮，並說明談判結果較第八次增資削減 27%，或僅說明整體資源相對於綱要需求仍不足。","第 4 段對已開發締約方的用語是敦促還是請求。","第 11 段全球環境基金理事會應依第 16/34 號決定第 21 段的標準，還是依編號待定之新決定的標準；以及「包容」、「民主與透明」的治理字句，是否加入原住民族與地方社區、婦女與青年的充分有效參與。","第 12 段（d）、（e）、（f）、（g）、（h）、（i）與（o）各子段的用語仍有多個版本，包括資源分配制度的改進、直接取用原住民族與地方社區組織的程序與核准流程、區域倡議的核准程序，以及生物多樣性相關財務的報告標準。","第 23 段執行秘書為全球生物多樣性綱要基金階段性檢討（stocktake）所做的準備工作，是否依附件三辦理，並是否加註不預先判斷締約方大會對第 21 條未來制度結構的考量。","第 27 段是否通過附件一的額外指引；目前附件一僅為占位符，尚未擬定內容。","第 34 段鼓勵或邀請締約方建立協調機制或國家規劃平台，以及第 35 段是否通過第七次四年一度檢視的職權範圍（附件三），仍有不同版本。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p001.md","en":"                                                                                      CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n                                                                                    Distr.: Limited\n                                                                                    28 October 2026\n                                                                                    Original: English\n\n\n\n\nConference of the Parties to the\nConvention on Biological Diversity\nSeventeenth meeting\nYerevan, 19–30 October 2026\nAgenda item 8 (b)\nResource mobilization and financial\nmechanism: financial mechanism\nWorking Group I\n\n       Financial mechanism\n       Draft decision submitted by the Chair of Working Group I\n\n               The Conference of the Parties,\n              Recalling its decisions 15/15 of 19 December 2022 and 16/33 of 27 February 2025 pertaining\n       to the assessment of funding needed by all eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least\n       developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition for\n       the implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity 1 and its Protocols for the ninth\n       replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2026–June 2030),\n              Recalling also the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme\n       priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global\n       Environment Facility Trust Fund contained in annex I to decision 16/33,\n              Recognizing that the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework2 is relevant to all\n       biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements and the mandate\n       of the Global Environment Facility,\n             [1. [Welcomes][Acknowledges][Notes with appreciation] the pledges made as at 30 May\n       2026 for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by participant\n       countries, namely, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, China, Côte d’Ivoire, France,\n       Germany, India, Ireland, Italy, Japan, Luxembourg, Mexico, Netherlands (Kingdom of the), New\n       Zealand, Norway, Slovenia, South Africa, Switzerland and Uzbekistan, which amounted to\n       approximately 3.9 billion United States dollars, using the agreed reference exchange rates for the\n       replenishment period;3]\n             [2. Notes with concern that the amount of 3.9 billion dollars is contributed by only 50 per\n       cent of developed country Parties, and appreciates the contributions of developing country Parties,\n       namely, Brazil, China, Côte d’Ivoire, India, Mexico, South Africa and Uzbekistan;4]\n            [3. [Notes with deep concern] that [the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the\n       Global Environment Facility Trust Fund concluded with a reduction of 27 per cent compared with\n\n1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n2 Decision 15/4, annex.\n3 To be updated in October 2026.\n4 To be updated in October 2026.","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n發行：有限\n2026年10月28日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13<br />\n發行：有限<br />\n2026年10月28日<br />\n原文：英文</p>"},{"md":"生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第十七次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19日至30日\n議程項目 8 (b)\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制\n第一工作小組","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第十七次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19日至30日<br />\n議程項目 8 (b)<br />\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制<br />\n第一工作小組</p>"},{"md":"財務機制\n由第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案\n締約方大會，","html":"<p>財務機制<br />\n由第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案<br />\n締約方大會，</p>"},{"md":"**回顧**其關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，為執行《生物多樣性公約》¹及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026年7月至2030年6月）所需資金之決定 15/15（2022年12月19日）及 16/33（2025年2月27日），","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，為執行《生物多樣性公約》¹及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026年7月至2030年6月）所需資金之決定 15/15（2022年12月19日）及 16/33（2025年2月27日），</p>"},{"md":"**亦回顧**決定 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，該公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>決定 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，該公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，</p>"},{"md":"**認識到**《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》²與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》²與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關，</p>"},{"md":"[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝並注意到] 截至2026年5月30日止，參與國為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間約定之參考匯率計算，總計約39億美元；³]","html":"<p>[1. [歡迎][承認][表示感謝並注意到] 截至2026年5月30日止，參與國為全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭（王國）、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、瑞士及烏茲別克，其金額依增資期間約定之參考匯率計算，總計約39億美元；³]</p>"},{"md":"[2. **憂心地注意到** 39億美元之金額僅由50%的開發國家締約方所貢獻，並**感謝**開發中國家締約方的貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；⁴]","html":"<p>[2. <strong>憂心地注意到</strong> 39億美元之金額僅由50%的開發國家締約方所貢獻，並<strong>感謝</strong>開發中國家締約方的貢獻，即：巴西、中國、象牙海岸、印度、墨西哥、南非及烏茲別克；⁴]</p>"},{"md":"[3. [**深切憂心地注意到**] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判，與第八次增資期相比減少了27%","html":"<p>[3. [<strong>深切憂心地注意到</strong>] [全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判，與第八次增資期相比減少了27%</p>"},{"md":"---\n¹ 聯合國，條約集，第1760卷，第30619號。\n² 決定 15/4，附件。\n³ 待2026年10月更新。\n⁴ 待2026年10月更新。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹ 聯合國，條約集，第1760卷，第30619號。<br />\n² 決定 15/4，附件。<br />\n³ 待2026年10月更新。<br />\n⁴ 待2026年10月更新。</p>"}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p002.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n       the eighth replenishment period and that such a reduction comes at a time when Parties are expected\n       to accelerate the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework][the\n       overall level of resources remains insufficient in the light of the scale of needs to implement the\n       Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity\n       Framework, in particular Target 19 (a);]]5\n             4.    [Urges][Requests] developed country Parties, and invites other Parties that voluntarily\n       assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other countries, to make contributions for\n       the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund in support of the full\n       implementation of the Framework and in accordance with the provisions of Article 20 of the\n       Convention;\n             5.    Welcomes the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the\n       seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;6\n              6.    Also welcomes the improved disaggregation of co-financing by source in the report of\n       the Council of the Global Environment Facility and encourages the Facility to continue to enhance\n       the transparency and granularity of future reporting on the various sources of co-financing;\n             7.     Notes with appreciation that the programming directions for the ninth replenishment\n       period have been designed to deliver on all elements of the four-year outcome-oriented framework\n       of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment\n       period adopted by the Conference of the Parties at its sixteenth meeting,7 reflecting the effective\n       response to the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;\n             8.     Welcomes the allocation of 35 per cent of the ninth replenishment resources to the\n       biodiversity focal area, which is the largest focal area, and the aim of committing at least 70 per cent\n       of funding to biodiversity over that period, according to the Rio marker methodology of the\n       Development Assistance Committee of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and\n       Development;\n              9.     Also welcomes the inclusion in the programming directions and policy\n       recommendations of the Global Environment Facility for the ninth replenishment period of the\n       indigenous people and local community conservation initiative, 8 an aspirational target of\n       programming 20 per cent of resources to support indigenous peoples and local communities and\n       strengthened support to least developed countries and small island developing States, with an\n       aspirational benchmark of 35 per cent for those countries, as well as the introduction of the\n       aspirational target of programming 25 per cent to mobilize private capital;\n              10. Further welcomes the establishment of the Ad Hoc Governance Working Group of the\n       Council of the Global Environment Facility under the ninth replenishment of the Facility, in response\n       to decision 16/33;\n              [11. Requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria\n       [set out in paragraph 21 of decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025] [and decision 17/--], ensuring a\n\n5 Operative paragraphs 1 to 3 were considered at the seventh meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation (see\n\nrecommendation 7/3). Recommendation 6/2, adopted at its sixth meeting, also contained a paragraph on the topic of the ninth\nreplenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (para. 6), but that paragraph was not discussed at that\nmeeting. It is the understanding of the Secretariat that paragraphs 1 to 3 above reflect the discussions of the Subsidiary Body on\nthe subject and therefore supersede the not-negotiated paragraph 6 in recommendation 6/2. As a result, that paragraph has not\nbeen included in the present draft decision. For reference, it read as follows: “[Reiterates its appreciation to developed country\nParties, other Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other donors that contributed\nactively to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\nin support of eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States,\n[the most environmentally vulnerable country Parties,] and Parties with economies in transition;]”.\n6 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n7 Decision 16/33, annex I.\n8 Building on previous iterations of the Inclusive Conservation Initiative at an expanded level of 100 million dollars,\n\n\n\n2/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"且此類減幅發生在締約方預期應加速落實《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際][鑑於落實《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，資源總量仍顯不足；]]⁵","html":"<p>且此類減幅發生在締約方預期應加速落實《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際][鑑於落實《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》（特別是目標 19 (a)）之需求規模，資源總量仍顯不足；]]⁵</p>"},{"md":"4.\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方及其他國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補提供捐助，以支持綱要之全面落實，並符合公約第二十條之規定；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n[敦促][請求] 已開發國家締約方，並邀請其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方及其他國家，為全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補提供捐助，以支持綱要之全面落實，並符合公約第二十條之規定；</p>"},{"md":"5.\n歡迎全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所提交之報告；⁶","html":"<p>5.<br />\n歡迎全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所提交之報告；⁶</p>"},{"md":"6.\n亦歡迎全球環境基金理事會報告中，對共同融資來源之細分有所改善，並鼓勵基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細緻度；","html":"<p>6.<br />\n亦歡迎全球環境基金理事會報告中，對共同融資來源之細分有所改善，並鼓勵基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細緻度；</p>"},{"md":"7.\n注意到並表示讚賞，第九次增資期之規劃方向，旨在落實締約方大會於第十六次會議所採納之、為期四年且以成果為導向之公約及其議定書生物多樣性優先事項框架之所有要素⁷，反映了對締約方所提供之指引之有效回應；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n注意到並表示讚賞，第九次增資期之規劃方向，旨在落實締約方大會於第十六次會議所採納之、為期四年且以成果為導向之公約及其議定書生物多樣性優先事項框架之所有要素⁷，反映了對締約方所提供之指引之有效回應；</p>"},{"md":"8.\n歡迎將第九次增補資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標為在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n歡迎將第九次增補資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標為在該期間內將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；</p>"},{"md":"9.\n亦歡迎在全球環境基金第九次增資期之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議⁸，其目標為規劃 20% 的資源以支持原住民族與地方社區，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（其目標基準為 35%），以及引入規劃 25% 之資源以動員私人資本之願景目標；","html":"<p>9.<br />\n亦歡迎在全球環境基金第九次增資期之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議⁸，其目標為規劃 20% 的資源以支持原住民族與地方社區，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（其目標基準為 35%），以及引入規劃 25% 之資源以動員私人資本之願景目標；</p>"},{"md":"10. 進一步歡迎在全球環境基金第九次增補下，根據決定 16/33，成立全球環境基金理事會特設治理工作小組；","html":"<p>10. 進一步歡迎在全球環境基金第九次增補下，根據決定 16/33，成立全球環境基金理事會特設治理工作小組；</p>"},{"md":"[11. 請求全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決定 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決定 17/--]之標準，並確保一個","html":"<p>[11. 請求全球環境基金理事會考慮[於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決定 16/34 第 21 段所列之][及決定 17/--]之標準，並確保一個</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"⁵ 執行附屬機構第七次會議曾審議執行段落 1 至 3（參見建議 7/3）。於其第六次會議採納之建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期之主題（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議上進行討論。秘書處之理解為，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代了建議 6/2 中尚未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方，以及積極捐助全球生物多樣性綱要基金與全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補，以支持合資格之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中之締約方，之捐助者表示感謝；]」。","html":"<p>⁵ 執行附屬機構第七次會議曾審議執行段落 1 至 3（參見建議 7/3）。於其第六次會議採納之建議 6/2 亦包含一段關於全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期之主題（第 6 段），但該段落未在該次會議上進行討論。秘書處之理解為，上述第 1 至 3 段反映了附屬機構就該主題之討論，因此取代了建議 6/2 中尚未經談判之第 6 段。因此，該段落未包含在本決議草案中。供參考，其原文如下：「[重申對已開發國家締約方、其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方，以及積極捐助全球生物多樣性綱要基金與全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補，以支持合資格之開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家、[環境最脆弱之締約方] 以及經濟轉型中之締約方，之捐助者表示感謝；]」。</p>"},{"md":"⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。\n⁷ 決定 16/33，附件 I。\n⁸ 在將包容性保育倡議擴大至 1 億美元規模的基礎上，","html":"<p>⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。<br />\n⁷ 決定 16/33，附件 I。<br />\n⁸ 在將包容性保育倡議擴大至 1 億美元規模的基礎上，</p>"},{"md":"2/13","html":"<p>2/13</p>"}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p003.md","en":"                                                                                                   CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n       democratic and transparent system of governance that is fair, equitable, inclusive, efficient and\n       representative[, while facilitating the full and effective participation of indigenous people and local\n       communities, women and youth];]\n              12. Requests the Global Environment Facility to accelerate efforts to further strengthen its\n       effectiveness, including by:\n             (a) Improving integration pathways, approaches and integrated programmes that deliver\n       system-wide environmental benefits to improve synergies among environmental conventions, while\n       ensuring that such programmes take into account their respective mandates, remain country-driven,\n       responsive to national circumstances and priorities, and implemented through meaningful\n       engagement with national executing agencies from recipient countries;\n              (b) Enabling and facilitating private sector financing aligned with the objectives of the\n       Convention through its blended finance programme funding window and the provision of predictable\n       support to eligible Parties, with a view to developing projects and programmes that enable greater\n       private sector investment and financial flows, including through long-term enabling policy\n       frameworks, incentives, regulations, blended finance tools and the development of financially viable,\n       investment-ready biodiversity finance projects and pipelines, while recognizing that such\n       investments complement public finance;\n             (c) Promoting whole-of-society and whole-of-government approaches, as appropriate and\n       in accordance with national circumstances, to strengthen programme and project ownership at the\n       national level and the alignment of biodiversity actions with nationally identified priorities, national\n       biodiversity strategies and action plans, national development priorities, and policy coherence;\n              (d) Continuing to improve its system of resource allocation[9] [[, including by continuing\n       to maximize the generation of global environmental benefits and recognizing the role of indigenous\n       peoples and local communities in achieving them, and to improve the allocation performance of its\n       implementing entities] [by enhancing transparency, equity, predictability and responsiveness to the\n       [relevant][specific] needs and priorities of developing country Parties, including small island\n       developing States and least developed countries]];\n              (e) Sustaining enhanced support for all eligible Parties, in particular least developed\n       countries, small island developing States [and the most environmentally vulnerable countries], by\n       reducing transaction costs, simplifying access procedures across existing Global Environment\n       Facility focal areas and financing windows[, including through direct access modalities via national\n       implementing agencies,] and improving the timeliness and predictability of financial support,\n       measured by the date of first disbursement to the recipient country;\n              (f)   Deepening accessible support for indigenous peoples and local communities, in line\n       with element 8 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention\n       related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 203010 (access, including direct access, to\n       funding for indigenous peoples and local communities for the conservation, restoration and\n       sustainable use of biodiversity), including by developing guidance on the 20 per cent portfolio-wide\n       target for indigenous peoples and local communities, which includes the [dedicated][[direct]\n       access][11] modalities;\n\n\n\n[9 Ensuring that any performance-based element of the allocation formula, including any measure of past disbursement, does not\ndisadvantage Parties the disbursement rates of which reflect the capacity constraints that the financial mechanism exists to\nrelieve, consistent with paragraph 4 of Article 20 of the Convention.]\n10 Decision 16/4, annex.\n\n[11 Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities includes the application of procedures for screening\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to established\nGlobal Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global Environment Facility,\nwhich is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n\n                                                                                                                              3/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"民主且透明的治理制度，且該制度應具備公平、公正、包容、高效與代表性[，同時促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之充分且有效參與]；]","html":"<p>民主且透明的治理制度，且該制度應具備公平、公正、包容、高效與代表性[，同時促進原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之充分且有效參與]；]</p>"},{"md":"12. **請求**全球環境基金加速努力以進一步強化其成效，包括透過：","html":"<p>12. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金加速努力以進一步強化其成效，包括透過：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 改進整合路徑、方法及整合計畫，以提供全系統性的環境效益，藉此增進環境公約之間的綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自的職權，保持由國家驅動，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來執行；","html":"<p>(a) 改進整合路徑、方法及整合計畫，以提供全系統性的環境效益，藉此增進環境公約之間的綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自的職權，保持由國家驅動，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構之實質參與來執行；</p>"},{"md":"(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，以及向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，使符合《公約》目標之私部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目標在於開發能實現更大規模私部門投資與資金流動之計畫與項目，包括透過長期之賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具投資準備就緒之生物多樣性金融計畫與案源，同時承認此類投資係對公共財政之補充；","html":"<p>(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，以及向符合條件之締約方提供可預測之支持，使符合《公約》目標之私部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目標在於開發能實現更大規模私部門投資與資金流動之計畫與項目，包括透過長期之賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具投資準備就緒之生物多樣性金融計畫與案源，同時承認此類投資係對公共財政之補充；</p>"},{"md":"(c) 在適當且符合國家情況之情況下，推動全社會與全政府之方法，以強化國家層級之計畫與項目所有權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家所識別之優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性相結合；","html":"<p>(c) 在適當且符合國家情況之情況下，推動全社會與全政府之方法，以強化國家層級之計畫與項目所有權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家所識別之優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性相結合；</p>"},{"md":"(d) 持續改進其資源配置制度[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益之產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在達成該等效益中所扮演之角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應性]]；","html":"<p>(d) 持續改進其資源配置制度[9] [[，包括透過持續極大化全球環境效益之產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在達成該等效益中所扮演之角色，以及改善其執行實體之配置績效] [藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，並對開發中國家締約方（包括小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家）之[相關][特定]需求與優先事項之回應性]]；</p>"},{"md":"(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與資助窗口之取得程序[，包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，]，並改善財務支持之及時性與可預測性（以對受援國之首次撥款日期衡量），以持續為所有符合條件之締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]提供強化之支持；","html":"<p>(e) 透過降低交易成本、簡化現有全球環境基金焦點領域與資助窗口之取得程序[，包括透過國家執行機構之直接取得模式，]，並改善財務支持之及時性與可預測性（以對受援國之首次撥款日期衡量），以持續為所有符合條件之締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家[及環境最脆弱之國家]提供強化之支持；</p>"},{"md":"(f) 根據第八條(j)工作計畫之要素 8，以及《公約》中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他條款，深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得支持至 2030 年¹⁰（包括針對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過針對原住民族與地方社區之 20% 全組合目標開發指引，該目標包含[專用][[直接]取得][11]模式；","html":"<p>(f) 根據第八條(j)工作計畫之要素 8，以及《公約》中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他條款，深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得支持至 2030 年¹⁰（包括針對原住民族與地方社區用於生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用之資金取得，包含直接取得），包括透過針對原住民族與地方社區之 20% 全組合目標開發指引，該目標包含[專用][[直接]取得][11]模式；</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"[9 確保配置公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款量之衡量）不會對撥款率反映出財務機制旨在緩解之能力限制之締約方造成不利，此應與《公約》第二十條第四段保持一致。]\n10 決定 16/4，附件。\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，並經全球環境基金之營運焦點人員核准（該核准係與《公約》國家焦點人員協調進行），對組織管理資金與執行項目之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序之應用。]","html":"<p>[9 確保配置公式中任何以績效為基礎之要素（包括任何對過去撥款量之衡量）不會對撥款率反映出財務機制旨在緩解之能力限制之締約方造成不利，此應與《公約》第二十條第四段保持一致。]<br />\n10 決定 16/4，附件。<br />\n[11 原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定之全球環境基金程序，並經全球環境基金之營運焦點人員核准（該核准係與《公約》國家焦點人員協調進行），對組織管理資金與執行項目之能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序之應用。]</p>"}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p004.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n              [(g) Strengthening the full, equitable, inclusive, effective and gender-responsive\n       participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth[, including in decision-\n       making,] in accordance with the national legislation of concerned Parties;]\n              (h) Continuing to promote country-driven national initiatives and regionally coordinated\n       regional and multi-country initiatives[, including transboundary initiatives, with effective\n       participation [and formal approval] [of national focal points for the Convention and relevant national\n       authorities] [and formal approval of operational focal points for the Global Environment Facility]];\n             (i)    Ensuring that Global Environment Facility support for the implementation of the\n       Convention[, including support [through direct access [ 12 ]] for the implementation, monitoring,\n       update and review of national biodiversity strategies and action plans,] is country-led and aligned\n       with [national biodiversity strategies and action plans and] the targets of the Framework;\n             (j)     Continuing to support the development and implementation of national biodiversity\n       finance plans or similar instruments and their integration, where applicable, into national policies\n       and priorities;\n             (k) Continuing to advance collaboration, coherence and complementarity across\n       multilateral climate funds and other sources of finance relevant to the implementation of the\n       Framework;\n            (l)    Strengthening national institutional and technical capacities for project preparation,\n       implementation, monitoring and reporting;\n               [(m) Simplifying project development guidance;]\n             (n) Reporting on the attainment of the targets mentioned in paragraph 9 above and on\n       disaggregated data on programming, approvals and disbursement by recipient country or region;\n             [(o) Improving the transparency and granularity of reporting on biodiversity-related finance,\n       including by distinguishing between financing for which biodiversity is a principal objective and\n       financing for which it is a significant objective under the Rio marker methodology, taking into\n       account the qualitative nature of the Rio markers and by clarifying the extent to which such financing\n       contribute to the implementation of the Framework;]\n               13. Also requests the Global Environment Facility to report to the Conference of the Parties\n       at its eighteenth meeting on the resources of the biodiversity focal area for the ninth replenishment\n       period of its Trust Fund expressed in United States dollars at the final replenishment level, together\n       with the corresponding figure for the eighth replenishment period, and on the share of resources\n       originally programmed and subsequently disbursed to small island developing States, presented\n       separately from least developed countries;\n             14. Recognizes the value of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund in complementing the\n       Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by providing financial support to eligible developing\n       country Parties for achieving the goals and targets of the Framework;\n             15. Welcomes the progress made by the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund with a one-\n       step approval process and the achievement to date of the three portfolio targets set forth in the\n       programming directions for the Fund;13\n             16. Takes note of the information on the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund contained in\n       the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the\n       Conference of the Parties;\n\n12 [Direct access for organizations of indigenous peoples and local communities include application of procedures for screening\n\nthe capacities, experience and performance of organizations in managing funds and implementing projects, according to\nestablished Global Environment Facility procedures and following approval by the operational focal points of the Global\nEnvironment Facility, which is granted in coordination with the national focal point for the Convention.]\n13 Global Environment Facility, document GEF/C.64/06/Rev/02.\n\n\n\n4/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"[(g) 根據相關締約方的國家立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年[，包括在決策中，]之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性的參與；]\n(h) 持續推動由國家主導的國家倡議，以及區域性且多國協調的區域與多國倡議[，包括跨境倡議，並在[國家公約聯絡點及相關國家主管機關]之有效參與[與正式核准][以及全球環境基金執行聯絡點之正式核准]下進行]；\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對履行公約之支持[，包括[透過直接取得[ 12 ]]對國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之執行、監測、更新與審查提供支持，]應由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及]綱要之目標保持一致；\n(j) 持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具之制定與執行，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；\n(k) 持續推進多邊氣候基金與其他與履行綱要相關之財務來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；\n(l) 強化國家在專案準備、執行、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；\n[(m) 簡化專案開發指南；]\n(n) 報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之計畫編列、核准與撥款的細分資料；\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標之融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標之融資，並考量里約標記的性質，且澄清此類融資在多大程度上對履行綱要有所貢獻；]","html":"<p>[(g) 根據相關締約方的國家立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年[，包括在決策中，]之全面、公平、包容、有效且具性別回應性的參與；]<br />\n(h) 持續推動由國家主導的國家倡議，以及區域性且多國協調的區域與多國倡議[，包括跨境倡議，並在[國家公約聯絡點及相關國家主管機關]之有效參與[與正式核准][以及全球環境基金執行聯絡點之正式核准]下進行]；<br />\n(i) 確保全球環境基金對履行公約之支持[，包括[透過直接取得[ 12 ]]對國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之執行、監測、更新與審查提供支持，]應由國家主導，並與[國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及]綱要之目標保持一致；<br />\n(j) 持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具之制定與執行，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；<br />\n(k) 持續推進多邊氣候基金與其他與履行綱要相關之財務來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；<br />\n(l) 強化國家在專案準備、執行、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；<br />\n[(m) 簡化專案開發指南；]<br />\n(n) 報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之計畫編列、核准與撥款的細分資料；<br />\n[(o) 提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標之融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標之融資，並考量里約標記的性質，且澄清此類融資在多大程度上對履行綱要有所貢獻；]</p>"},{"md":"13. 亦**請求**全球環境基金在其第十八次締約方大會上，就其信託基金第九次增資期間，以最終增資水平表示之美金計價之生物多樣性重點領域資源，連同第八次增資期間之相應數字，以及原先編列並隨後撥付給小島嶼開發中國家之資源比例進行報告，且該報告應與低度開發國家之報告分開呈現；","html":"<p>13. 亦<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金在其第十八次締約方大會上，就其信託基金第九次增資期間，以最終增資水平表示之美金計價之生物多樣性重點領域資源，連同第八次增資期間之相應數字，以及原先編列並隨後撥付給小島嶼開發中國家之資源比例進行報告，且該報告應與低度開發國家之報告分開呈現；</p>"},{"md":"14. **認識到**全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要之長期目標與目標；","html":"<p>14. <strong>認識到</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要之長期目標與目標；</p>"},{"md":"15. **歡迎**全球生物多樣性綱要基金透過單一步驟核准程序所取得的進展，以及迄今為止達成基金計畫編列方向中所設定之三項投資組合目標之成就；$^{13}$","html":"<p>15. <strong>歡迎</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金透過單一步驟核准程序所取得的進展，以及迄今為止達成基金計畫編列方向中所設定之三項投資組合目標之成就；<sup>13</sup></p>"},{"md":"16. **注意到**全球環境基金理事會於第十七次締約方大會報告中所包含之關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊；","html":"<p>16. <strong>注意到</strong>全球環境基金理事會於第十七次締約方大會報告中所包含之關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊；</p>"},{"md":"$^{12}$ [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定的全球環境基金程序，針對組織在管理基金與執行專案方面的能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序申請，且須在與公約國家聯絡點協調下，經全球環境基金執行聯絡點核准後授予。]\n$^{13}$ 全球環境基金，文件 GEF/C.64/06/Rev/02。","html":"<p><sup>12</sup> [原住民族與地方社區組織之直接取得，包括根據既定的全球環境基金程序，針對組織在管理基金與執行專案方面的能力、經驗與績效進行篩選之程序申請，且須在與公約國家聯絡點協調下，經全球環境基金執行聯絡點核准後授予。]<br />\n<sup>13</sup> 全球環境基金，文件 GEF/C.64/06/Rev/02。</p>"}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p005.md","en":"                                                                                     CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n              17. Recalls paragraph 14 of decision 16/33, emphasizing the need to further scale up new\n        and additional resources from all sources to match the ambition of the Kunming-Montreal Global\n        Biodiversity Framework, in accordance with paragraphs 19 and 20 of decision 15/15, while\n        recognizing that many eligible Parties have not yet received support from the Fund;\n               18. Reiterates the call made by the Council of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund at\n        its sixth meeting for new and additional contributions from all sources to support the continuous,\n        rapid and robust capitalization of the Fund, in line with Target 19 of the Kunming-Montreal Global\n        Biodiversity Framework and without affecting existing obligations under Article 20 of the\n        Convention;\n               19. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund to enhance efforts to mobilize\n        predictable, adequate and additional resources from all sources and report on the implementation of\n        its resource mobilization strategy for the period from July 2026 to June 2030, including through\n        disaggregated information on pledges and contributions paid by sources of finance;\n              20. Invites developed country Parties and Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of\n        developed country Parties, other governments at all levels, the private sector and philanthropic\n        organizations to make or increase their contributions to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;\n              21. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and its implementing agencies to\n        continue to enhance its efforts to:\n              (a) Facilitate, as appropriate, the mobilization of financial resources from all sources,\n        recognizing the need for further capitalization;\n                (b) Improve co-financing arrangements, as appropriate, while recognizing that co-financing\n        is not a requirement, without creating additional barriers to access or shifting the financial burden to\n        all eligible countries, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States,\n        and taking into consideration the specific needs of vulnerable countries, in the context of\n        paragraphs 6 and 7 of Article 20 of the Convention;\n              (c) Reduce, where appropriate and taking into account country ownership, project cycle\n        processing times, including for the disbursement and endorsement processes of approved projects,\n        through transparent, predictable and time-bound procedures, and streamline implementation;\n              (d) Report on average processing and disbursement times disaggregated for least developed\n        countries and small island developing States, and other eligible Parties by region;\n               [(e) Enhance equitable access, including by considering measures to facilitate access for [all]\n        eligible country Parties[, [including] [in particular] those] that [are yet to receive][have not yet\n        received] support from the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;]\n              22. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive\n        Secretary, to provide, within their respective mandates, support to [all] eligible Parties, upon request,\n        for:\n              (a) Project preparation, capacity-building and the tracking of ongoing biodiversity funding\n        needs, gaps and priorities, as necessary, including, where applicable, through national coordination\n        mechanisms, such as country platforms or national steering committees;\n             (b) The preparation and submission of national reports on the implementation of the\n        Convention, the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety14 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic\n        Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, taking into\n        account national circumstances;15\n\n\n\n14 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n15 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                            5/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"17. **回顧**決定 16/33 第 14 段，強調根據決定 15/15 第 19 段與第 20 段，有必要進一步擴大來自所有來源的新增與額外資源，以符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之雄心，同時承認許多符合資格的締約方尚未從該基金獲得支持；","html":"<p>17. <strong>回顧</strong>決定 16/33 第 14 段，強調根據決定 15/15 第 19 段與第 20 段，有必要進一步擴大來自所有來源的新增與額外資源，以符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之雄心，同時承認許多符合資格的締約方尚未從該基金獲得支持；</p>"},{"md":"18. **重申**全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在其第六次會議上所提出的呼籲，要求來自所有來源的新增與額外捐助，以支持該基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，並符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 19，且不影響《公約》第 20 條下既有的義務；","html":"<p>18. <strong>重申</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會在其第六次會議上所提出的呼籲，要求來自所有來源的新增與額外捐助，以支持該基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，並符合昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之目標 19，且不影響《公約》第 20 條下既有的義務；</p>"},{"md":"19. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略的實施情況，包括透過按財務來源分類的承諾與已支付捐助之細分資訊；","html":"<p>19. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強努力，從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外的資源，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略的實施情況，包括透過按財務來源分類的承諾與已支付捐助之細分資訊；</p>"},{"md":"20. **邀請**已開發國家締約方以及自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其捐助；","html":"<p>20. <strong>邀請</strong>已開發國家締約方以及自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其捐助；</p>"},{"md":"21. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：\n    (a) 在適當情況下，促進來自所有來源之財務資源的動員，並承認進一步資本化的必要性；\n    (b) 在適當情況下，改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成取得資源的額外障礙，亦不應將財務負擔轉嫁至所有符合資格的國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並在《公約》第 20 條第 6 段與第 7 段的背景下，考量脆弱國家的特定需求；\n    (c) 在適當情況下，並考量國家自主權，透過透明、可預測且有時限的程序，縮短專案週期處理時間，包括已核准專案的撥款與認可程序，並簡化實施流程；\n    (d) 報告按區域分類之低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及其他符合資格締約方的平均處理與撥款時間；\n    [(e) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施以促進 [所有] 符合資格之締約方[, [包括] [特別是] 那些] [尚未獲得][尚未從全球生物多樣性綱要基金獲得]支持之國家的取得；]","html":"<p>21. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：<br />\n    (a) 在適當情況下，促進來自所有來源之財務資源的動員，並承認進一步資本化的必要性；<br />\n    (b) 在適當情況下，改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成取得資源的額外障礙，亦不應將財務負擔轉嫁至所有符合資格的國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並在《公約》第 20 條第 6 段與第 7 段的背景下，考量脆弱國家的特定需求；<br />\n    (c) 在適當情況下，並考量國家自主權，透過透明、可預測且有時限的程序，縮短專案週期處理時間，包括已核准專案的撥款與認可程序，並簡化實施流程；<br />\n    (d) 報告按區域分類之低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及其他符合資格締約方的平均處理與撥款時間；<br />\n    [(e) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施以促進 [所有] 符合資格之締約方[, [包括] [特別是] 那些] [尚未獲得][尚未從全球生物多樣性綱要基金獲得]支持之國家的取得；]</p>"},{"md":"22. **請求**全球環境基金與執行秘書合作，在其各自的職權範圍內，應要求向 [所有] 符合資格的締約方提供以下支持：\n    (a) 視必要情況，進行專案準備、能力建構以及追蹤進行中的生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項，包括在適用時，透過國家協調機制（例如國家平台或國家指導委員會）；\n    (b) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於實施《公約》、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書$^{14}$以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其產生的利益之名古屋議定書》之國家報告$^{15}$；","html":"<p>22. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與執行秘書合作，在其各自的職權範圍內，應要求向 [所有] 符合資格的締約方提供以下支持：<br />\n    (a) 視必要情況，進行專案準備、能力建構以及追蹤進行中的生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項，包括在適用時，透過國家協調機制（例如國家平台或國家指導委員會）；<br />\n    (b) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於實施《公約》、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書<sup>14</sup>以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其產生的利益之名古屋議定書》之國家報告<sup>15</sup>；</p>"},{"md":"$^{14}$ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n$^{15}$ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p><sup>14</sup> 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n<sup>15</sup> 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p006.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n             (c) Capacity-building for leveraging private sector financing, including from capital\n       markets, through, inter alia, innovative mechanisms and blended finance, and for developing\n       financially viable projects, with robust environmental, social and financial safeguards, taking into\n       account debt vulnerabilities;\n              23. Requests the Executive Secretary to undertake preparatory work for the stocktake\n       review of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund referred to in paragraph 29 of decision 15/15,[\n       in accordance with annex III to the present decision], in conjunction with its seventh quadrennial\n       review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, [recognizing that the stocktake shall inform,\n       but not prejudge, consideration by the Conference of the Parties of the future institutional structure\n       of the financial mechanism provided under Article 21 of the Convention];\n              24. Requests the Global Environment Facility to facilitate the provision of financial support\n       for [all] eligible Parties in a timely manner for the development of national biodiversity strategies\n       and action plans and national targets and the preparation of eighth national reports by the eighteenth\n       meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n             25. Also requests the Global Environment Facility, in consultation with recipient countries\n       and the Executive Secretary, to review the effectiveness of projects funded during its seventh and\n       eighth cycles for the development of national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national\n       reports under the Convention and its Protocols and to report on the measures that it has taken to\n       address identified challenges for the preparation of the eighth national report to the Subsidiary Body\n       on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n              26. Requests the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Secretariat of the Global\n       Environment Facility, to prepare a draft four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity\n       programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols related to the use of Facility resources for\n       biodiversity for the period from July 2030 to June 2034, taking into consideration the global review\n       of collective progress in the implementation of the Framework, as well as access modalities and\n       capacity constraints of developing countries Parties, in particular least developed countries and small\n       island developing States, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting\n       held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and subsequent adoption by the\n       Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n              [27. Adopts the additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility contained in annex I\n       to the present decision, and requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to include\n       information regarding the implementation of the additional guidance in its reports to the Conference\n       of the Parties;]\n             28. Notes the information on funding needs received from 45 eligible Parties and the\n       compilation and analysis of that information transmitted by the Secretariat of the Convention on\n       Biological Diversity to the Global Environment Facility to help with the negotiations for the ninth\n       replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;\n             29. Takes note of the report on the assessment of the amount of funds needed for the\n       implementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global\n       Environment Facility Trust Fund;16\n              30. Notes the limited number of submissions from eligible Parties and therefore limited\n       information available for assessing the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the\n       Convention and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework for the\n       ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;\n\n\n\n\n16 CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.\n\n\n\n6/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"(c) 透過創新機制與混合金融等方式，強化槓桿化私部門融資（包括來自資本市場之融資）的能力建構，以及開發具備穩健環境、社會與財務保障且具財務可行性之專案，並考量債務脆弱性；","html":"<p>(c) 透過創新機制與混合金融等方式，強化槓桿化私部門融資（包括來自資本市場之融資）的能力建構，以及開發具備穩健環境、社會與財務保障且具財務可行性之專案，並考量債務脆弱性；</p>"},{"md":"23. **請求**執行秘書針對決定 15/15 第 29 段所提及之全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行清查審核展開準備工作，[依本決定附件 III 之規定]，並與其第七次財務機制成效四年一度審查一併進行，[並承認清查審核應為締約方大會對《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構之考量提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；","html":"<p>23. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書針對決定 15/15 第 29 段所提及之全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行清查審核展開準備工作，[依本決定附件 III 之規定]，並與其第七次財務機制成效四年一度審查一併進行，[並承認清查審核應為締約方大會對《公約》第 21 條規定之財務機制未來制度結構之考量提供資訊，但不應預設其結果]；</p>"},{"md":"24. **請求**全球環境基金及時為[所有]符合資格之締約方提供財務支持，以利於第十八次締約方大會召開前，完成國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標之制定，以及第八次國家報告之編製；","html":"<p>24. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金及時為[所有]符合資格之締約方提供財務支持，以利於第十八次締約方大會召開前，完成國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家目標之制定，以及第八次國家報告之編製；</p>"},{"md":"25. **亦請求**全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為開發《公約》及其議定書下之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助專案之成效，並於第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次執行附屬機構會議上，就其為應對已識別之挑戰所採取之措施進行報告；","html":"<p>25. <strong>亦請求</strong>全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為開發《公約》及其議定書下之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助專案之成效，並於第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次執行附屬機構會議上，就其為應對已識別之挑戰所採取之措施進行報告；</p>"},{"md":"26. **請求**執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量全球對於實施綱要集體進展之全球審查，以及開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，準備一份關於《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向架構草案，該架構與使用全球環境基金生物多樣性資源有關，期間為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月，以供執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議進行審議，並隨後由締約方大會於其第十八次會議上採納；","html":"<p>26. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量全球對於實施綱要集體進展之全球審查，以及開發中締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，準備一份關於《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期成果導向架構草案，該架構與使用全球環境基金生物多樣性資源有關，期間為 2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月，以供執行附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議進行審議，並隨後由締約方大會於其第十八次會議上採納；</p>"},{"md":"[27. 採納本決定附件 I 中包含之給予全球環境基金之額外指引，並請求全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關實施該額外指引之資訊；]","html":"<p>[27. 採納本決定附件 I 中包含之給予全球環境基金之額外指引，並請求全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關實施該額外指引之資訊；]</p>"},{"md":"28. **注意到**來自 45 個符合資格之締約方所提交之資金需求資訊，以及生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補之談判；","html":"<p>28. <strong>注意到</strong>來自 45 個符合資格之締約方所提交之資金需求資訊，以及生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金之該等資訊之彙編與分析，以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增補之談判；</p>"},{"md":"29. **注意到**關於全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額評估之報告；¹⁶","html":"<p>29. <strong>注意到</strong>關於全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額評估之報告；¹⁶</p>"},{"md":"30. **注意到**來自符合資格之締約方提交之文件數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要所需之資金金額，可得之資訊有限；","html":"<p>30. <strong>注意到</strong>來自符合資格之締約方提交之文件數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要所需之資金金額，可得之資訊有限；</p>"},{"md":"¹⁶ CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.","html":"<p>¹⁶ CBD/SBI/6/INF/13.</p>"}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p007.md","en":"                                                                          CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n      31. Also notes the importance of a realistic assessment of funding necessary and available\nfor the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Framework for future\nreplenishment periods of the Global Environment Facility;\n        32. Emphasizes the need to continue to strengthen technical and institutional support for\n[all] eligible Parties, so that their needs are fully reflected in future assessments;\n       33. Adopts the terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are\nnecessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small\nisland developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance\nprovided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention to\ninform, if appropriate, the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\n(July 2030–June 2034), as contained in annex II to the present decision, noting that the assessment\nshould be conducted in a manner that avoids disproportionate administrative burdens and provides\nfor financial and technical support for data collection in developing country Parties;\n       [34. [Encourages][Invites] Parties to establish [coordination mechanisms [, such as country\nplatforms]] [national planning platforms] for planning and monitoring biodiversity projects that are\naccessible to stakeholders and regularly updated;]\n       [35. Adopts the terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of\nthe financial mechanism, as contained in annex III to the present decision;]\n       36. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations, as well as indigenous\npeoples and local communities, women and youth, to contribute to and participate in the seventh\nquadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as outlined in the terms of\nreference;\n       37. Emphasizes the importance of integrating in the quadrennial review specific indicators\nfor [all] eligible Parties, in particular on the number of projects funded, disbursement times and\nimpact on local communities;\n      38.    Requests the Executive Secretary:\n        (a) To commission and make available a report on the seventh quadrennial review of the\neffectiveness of the financial mechanism in time for consideration by the Conference of the Parties\nat its eighteenth meeting;\n       (b) To prepare a report on the full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to\nassist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island\ndeveloping States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance\nprovided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for\nthe tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, for consideration by\nthe Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the\nConference of the Parties and by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;\n     (c) Subject to the availability of resources, to further strengthen collaboration and\nengagement with relevant financial institutions and stakeholders, in order to accelerate the\nimplementation of the Framework, with an emphasis on improving access modalities;\n       (d) To report, as applicable, on the results of the collaboration and engagement mentioned\nin the subparagraph above, and include options for such engagements, to the Subsidiary Body on\nImplementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n        (e) To facilitate, as applicable, the effective participation of indigenous peoples and local\ncommunities, women and youth in the implementation of the activities referred to in subparagraphs\n(a) to (d) above.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                7/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"31. 亦**注意到**，為了在全球環境基金未來增補週期中，對履行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用資金進行務實評估的重要性；\n32. **強調**有必要繼續加強對[所有]符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以便其需求能充分反映在未來的評估中；\n33. **採納**如本決定附件 II 所載之任務說明，針對為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，以履行其在《公約》下之承諾，進行關於所需資金總額之全面評估，以利全球環境基金信託基金第十次增補週期（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）之適當通報；並**注意到**該評估應以避免不成比例之行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中國家締約方之資料收集提供財務與技術支持；\n[34. [鼓勵][邀請]締約方建立[協調機制[, 例如國家平台]] [國家規劃平台]，用於規劃與監測生物多樣性專案，且該平台應為利害關係人所能取得並定期更新；]\n[35. 採納如本決定附件 III 所載之關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之任務說明；]\n36. **邀請**締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為任務說明中所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；\n37. **強調**在四年一度審查中，針對[所有]符合資格締約方納入特定指標之重要性，特別是關於資助專案數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；\n38. **請求**執行秘書：","html":"<p>31. 亦<strong>注意到</strong>，為了在全球環境基金未來增補週期中，對履行《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用資金進行務實評估的重要性；<br />\n32. <strong>強調</strong>有必要繼續加強對[所有]符合資格締約方的技術與制度支持，以便其需求能充分反映在未來的評估中；<br />\n33. <strong>採納</strong>如本決定附件 II 所載之任務說明，針對為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，以履行其在《公約》下之承諾，進行關於所需資金總額之全面評估，以利全球環境基金信託基金第十次增補週期（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）之適當通報；並<strong>注意到</strong>該評估應以避免不成比例之行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中國家締約方之資料收集提供財務與技術支持；<br />\n[34. [鼓勵][邀請]締約方建立[協調機制[, 例如國家平台]] [國家規劃平台]，用於規劃與監測生物多樣性專案，且該平台應為利害關係人所能取得並定期更新；]<br />\n[35. 採納如本決定附件 III 所載之關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之任務說明；]<br />\n36. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府與相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為任務說明中所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；<br />\n37. <strong>強調</strong>在四年一度審查中，針對[所有]符合資格締約方納入特定指標之重要性，特別是關於資助專案數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；<br />\n38. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；\n(b) 準備一份關於為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，以履行其在《公約》下之承諾，針對全球環境基金信託基金第十次增補週期所需資金總額之全面評估報告，以供執行附屬機構在締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；\n(c) 在資源可用的情況下，進一步加強與相關金融機構及利害關係人之協作與參與，以加速《綱要》之實施，並著重於改善取得模式；\n(d) 視情況就上述子段落所述之協作與參與結果進行報告，並向執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之會議提出此類參與之選項；\n(e) 視情況促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 子段落所述活動之實施。","html":"<p>(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；<br />\n(b) 準備一份關於為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及轉型經濟體締約方，依據締約方所提供之指引，以履行其在《公約》下之承諾，針對全球環境基金信託基金第十次增補週期所需資金總額之全面評估報告，以供執行附屬機構在締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；<br />\n(c) 在資源可用的情況下，進一步加強與相關金融機構及利害關係人之協作與參與，以加速《綱要》之實施，並著重於改善取得模式；<br />\n(d) 視情況就上述子段落所述之協作與參與結果進行報告，並向執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之會議提出此類參與之選項；<br />\n(e) 視情況促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 子段落所述活動之實施。</p>"}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p008.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n       Annex I\n       Additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility\n                       [Placeholder for elements of guidance]\n       Annex II\n       Terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to\n       assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and\n       small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in\n       accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling\n       their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the\n       Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034)\n       A.      Objective and scope\n       1.    The objective of the work to be carried out under the present terms of reference is to enable\n       the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity17 to make an assessment of\n       the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least\n       developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in\n       accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their\n       commitments under the Convention and its Protocols, in particular the commitment to implementing\n       any successor to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework 18 over the tenth\n       replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034), and\n       determine the amount of resources needed, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the\n       Convention and decision III/8 of 15 November 1996 of the Conference of the Parties.\n       B.      Methodology\n       2.      The funding needs assessment should be conducted taking into account:\n               (a)     Article 20 and paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention, as well as the Framework;\n            (b) Guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties, which\n       may call for future financial resources, and in the resource mobilization decision, in which the\n       Conference of the Parties calls for a broadening of the contributor base;\n             (c) All obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and relevant decisions adopted\n       by the Conference of the Parties, in particular the Framework;\n            (d) National strategies, plans or programmes developed in accordance with Article 6 of the\n       Convention and national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments, where available;\n              (e) Information communicated to the Conference of the Parties in national reports and by\n       the Parties through the financial reporting framework and other submission responses to surveys and\n       interviews;\n             (f)   Policies and guidelines agreed by the Council of the Global Environment Facility for\n       determining eligibility for funding of projects;\n             (g) Synergies with other biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral\n       environmental agreements funded by the Global Environment Facility, including those with respect\n       to operations and impacts;\n             (h) Additional private capital mobilized through blended finance, including through the use\n       of non-grant instruments, while recognizing the challenges that may be experienced by some Parties,\n\n\n17 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n18 Decision 15/4, annex.\n\n\n\n8/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"附件 I\n給全球環境基金之額外指引\n[指引要素之預留位置]","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n給全球環境基金之額外指引<br />\n[指引要素之預留位置]</p>"},{"md":"附件 II\n關於根據締約方大會所提供之指引，為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，在全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期（2030年7月至2034年6月）期間，履行其在《公約》下之承諾，進行必要資金金額之全面評估之任務說明書","html":"<p>附件 II<br />\n關於根據締約方大會所提供之指引，為協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，在全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期（2030年7月至2034年6月）期間，履行其在《公約》下之承諾，進行必要資金金額之全面評估之任務說明書</p>"},{"md":"A.","html":"<p>A.</p>"},{"md":"目標與範圍","html":"<p>目標與範圍</p>"},{"md":"1.\n根據本任務說明書所進行之工作，其目標在於使《生物多樣性公約》¹⁷之締約方大會能夠進行評估，以確定在全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期（2030年7月至2034年6月）期間，根據締約方大會所提供之指引，協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，履行其在《公約》及其議定書下之承諾，特別是實施「昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要」¹⁸之任何後續措施之承諾，並根據《公約》第21條第1段及1996年11月15日締約方大會第III/8號決定，確定所需資源之金額。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據本任務說明書所進行之工作，其目標在於使《生物多樣性公約》¹⁷之締約方大會能夠進行評估，以確定在全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期（2030年7月至2034年6月）期間，根據締約方大會所提供之指引，協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，履行其在《公約》及其議定書下之承諾，特別是實施「昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要」¹⁸之任何後續措施之承諾，並根據《公約》第21條第1段及1996年11月15日締約方大會第III/8號決定，確定所需資源之金額。</p>"},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>"},{"md":"方法論","html":"<p>方法論</p>"},{"md":"2.\n資金需求評估應考量：\n(a) 《公約》第20條及第21條第1段，以及「綱要」；\n(b) 締約方大會提供予財務機制之指引（該指引可能要求未來之財務資源），以及在要求擴大出資者基礎之資源動員決定中之指引；\n(c) 《公約》及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決定，特別是「綱要」；\n(d) 根據《公約》第6條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；\n(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會通報之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於確定計畫資助資格之政策與指引；\n(g) 與其他由全球環境基金資助之生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議之協同效應，包括在運作與影響方面之協同效應；\n(h) 透過混合金融（包括透過使用非撥款工具）所動員之額外私人資本，同時承認某些締約方可能面臨之挑戰，","html":"<p>2.<br />\n資金需求評估應考量：<br />\n(a) 《公約》第20條及第21條第1段，以及「綱要」；<br />\n(b) 締約方大會提供予財務機制之指引（該指引可能要求未來之財務資源），以及在要求擴大出資者基礎之資源動員決定中之指引；<br />\n(c) 《公約》及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決定，特別是「綱要」；<br />\n(d) 根據《公約》第6條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；<br />\n(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會通報之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；<br />\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於確定計畫資助資格之政策與指引；<br />\n(g) 與其他由全球環境基金資助之生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議之協同效應，包括在運作與影響方面之協同效應；<br />\n(h) 透過混合金融（包括透過使用非撥款工具）所動員之額外私人資本，同時承認某些締約方可能面臨之挑戰，</p>"},{"md":"¹⁷ 聯合國，條約集，第1760卷，第30619號。\n¹⁸ 決定 15/4，附件。","html":"<p>¹⁷ 聯合國，條約集，第1760卷，第30619號。<br />\n¹⁸ 決定 15/4，附件。</p>"}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p009.md","en":"                                                                                    CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n        in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, in mobilizing private\n        capital in this regard;\n                (i)     Policy coherence;\n              (j)   Other relevant estimations, including the costs of implementing the Gender Plan of\n        Action (2023–2030);19\n              (k) Exchange rates, inflation and the incremental costs of the implementation of the\n        provisions of the Convention in developing countries.\n        3.    In the context of the assessment, interviews, surveys, quantitative and qualitative analyses, and\n        consultations should be undertaken, as needed for the preparation of the report, including:\n               (a) A compilation and analysis of the needs identified in national biodiversity strategies and\n        action plans and national biodiversity finance plans, including country-specific resource mobilization\n        strategies, prepared by Global Environment Facility-eligible and other relevant Parties pursuant to\n        Article 6 of the Convention, taking into account incremental cost funding as the fundamental\n        operational principle of the Global Environment Facility;\n               (b) A review of reports submitted by Parties pursuant to Articles 6 and 26 of the Convention,\n        as well as Article 33 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety20 and Article 29 of the Nagoya Protocol\n        on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their\n        Utilization, 21 to identify funding needs related to the fulfilment of their obligations under the\n        Convention and its Protocols;\n              (c) The estimated financial implications of guidance provided to the financial mechanism\n        by the Conference of the Parties;\n              (d) A compilation and analysis of any supplementary information provided by Global\n        Environment Facility-eligible Parties on their funding needs for the implementation of their\n        obligations under the Convention and its Protocols.\n        C.      Implementation\n        4.    The national focal points of the Convention and the focal points of the financial mechanism\n        should, as appropriate, bear joint responsibility for coordinating national-level incremental funding\n        needs assessments, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders and other focal points under the\n        Convention and related conventions to ensure a whole-of-government approach.\n        5.    The national focal points may establish a national platform or use existing national\n        coordination mechanisms, or both, to aid project planning, as necessary, and track ongoing\n        biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities. Close links should be established between the\n        national platform or relevant coordination mechanism and national support initiatives of relevant\n        funding providers, in particular the country engagement strategy of the Global Environment Facility.\n        6.    The national platform should also facilitate the participation of indigenous peoples and local\n        communities, women’s and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders, taking into account\n        section C of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, as appropriate, subject to\n        national legislation.\n        7.     The Executive Secretary should provide the information received from Parties without\n        additional reporting obligations on funding needs through an online platform, subject to the\n        availability of resources, to facilitate the visualization of biodiversity funding needs, gaps and\n        priorities on an ongoing basis.\n\n\n19 Decision 15/11, annex.\n20 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619.\n21 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619\n\n\n\n                                                                                                          9/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在該方面動員私人資本；","html":"<p>特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在該方面動員私人資本；</p>"},{"md":"(i) 政策一致性；","html":"<p>(i) 政策一致性；</p>"},{"md":"(j) 其他相關估算，包括實施性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；19","html":"<p>(j) 其他相關估算，包括實施性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；19</p>"},{"md":"(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹以及在開發中國家實施公約條款之增量成本。","html":"<p>(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹以及在開發中國家實施公約條款之增量成本。</p>"},{"md":"3.\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析以及諮商，包括：\n(a) 彙編並分析根據公約第六條，由符合全球環境基金資格之締約方及其他相關締約方所編製之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括特定國家的資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；\n(b) 審查締約方根據公約第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第三十三條與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》第二十九條所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在公約及其議定書下義務相關之資金需求；\n(c) 估算締約方大會向財務機制提供指引所產生的財務影響；\n(d) 彙編並分析符合全球環境基金資格之締約方，就履行其在公約及其議定書下義務之資金需求所提供之任何補充資訊。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析以及諮商，包括：<br />\n(a) 彙編並分析根據公約第六條，由符合全球環境基金資格之締約方及其他相關締約方所編製之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括特定國家的資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；<br />\n(b) 審查締約方根據公約第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第三十三條與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》第二十九條所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在公約及其議定書下義務相關之資金需求；<br />\n(c) 估算締約方大會向財務機制提供指引所產生的財務影響；<br />\n(d) 彙編並分析符合全球環境基金資格之締約方，就履行其在公約及其議定書下義務之資金需求所提供之任何補充資訊。</p>"},{"md":"C.\n實施","html":"<p>C.<br />\n實施</p>"},{"md":"4.\n公約之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點應視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資金需求評估，並與相關利害關係人及公約與相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，以確保採取全政府方法。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n公約之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點應視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資金需求評估，並與相關利害關係人及公約與相關公約下之其他聯絡點合作，以確保採取全政府方法。</p>"},{"md":"5.\n國家聯絡點可視需要建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助專案規劃，並追蹤持續進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。國家平台或相關協調機制，應與相關資金提供者之國家支持倡議建立緊密聯繫，特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n國家聯絡點可視需要建立國家平台或利用現有之國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助專案規劃，並追蹤持續進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。國家平台或相關協調機制，應與相關資金提供者之國家支持倡議建立緊密聯繫，特別是全球環境基金之國家參與策略。</p>"},{"md":"6.\n國家平台亦應在符合國家立法且視情況考慮《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》C節之前提下，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n國家平台亦應在符合國家立法且視情況考慮《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》C節之前提下，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。</p>"},{"md":"7.\n在資源可用之前提下，執行秘書應透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之關於資金需求且不涉及額外報告義務之資訊，以促進持續性地呈現生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項之視覺化。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n在資源可用之前提下，執行秘書應透過線上平台提供從締約方收到之關於資金需求且不涉及額外報告義務之資訊，以促進持續性地呈現生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項之視覺化。</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"19 決定 15/11，附件。\n20 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n21 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p>19 決定 15/11，附件。<br />\n20 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n21 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"},{"md":"9/13","html":"<p>9/13</p>"}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p010.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n        8.     The Executive Secretary should prepare a report on the full assessment, and the report should\n        be submitted for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before\n        the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, with a view to providing recommendations\n        for consideration by the Conference of the Parties at that meeting.\n        9.    At its eighteenth meeting, the Conference of the Parties will be invited to take note of the\n        estimated amount of funds that are necessary for the implementation of the Convention and its\n        Protocols for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund.\n\n        Annex III\n        Terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review\n        of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism\n        A.     Objectives\n        1.    In accordance with paragraph 3 of Article 21 of the Convention on Biological Diversity22 and\n        building upon the experience of the past six reviews of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism,\n        the Conference of the Parties to the Convention will undertake its seventh review at its eighteenth\n        meeting and take appropriate action to improve the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as\n        necessary. For that purpose, the following elements will be included in the review:\n               (a) The conformity of the activities of the Global Environment Facility, as the institutional\n        structure operating the financial mechanism, with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties;\n               (b) The effectiveness of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources to enable\n        eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island\n        developing States, and Parties with economies in transition to meet the agreed full incremental costs\n        to them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention\n        and its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits, and benefit from their provisions,\n        taking into account the need for predictability, adequacy, accessibility and timely flow of funds,\n        including the performance of the Global Environment Facility implementing agencies;\n               (c) The efficiency of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources and, in\n        accordance with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties, overseeing, monitoring and evaluating\n        the results of activities financed by its resources, including their social and gender- and equity-related\n        outcomes and impacts, as relevant;\n              (d) The effectiveness of catalysing and enhancing national implementation measures in line\n        with national priorities for achieving global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to\n        the Convention and its Protocols;\n               (e) The efficiency and effectiveness of the activities funded by the Global Environment\n        Facility and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund for the implementation of the Convention and\n        the achievement of its three objectives, as well as, as applicable, the implementation of its Protocols,\n        taking into account the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;\n               (f)   The efficiency and effectiveness of processes and procedures for the deployment and\n        use of resources, including simplified procedures and access modalities;\n              (g) The effectiveness and efficiency of the support provided for the objectives of the\n        Convention and its Protocols in synergy with the implementation of other relevant multilateral\n        environmental agreements, in a manner that is consistent with the mandates of the respective\n        agreements;\n\n\n\n\n22 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619.\n\n\n\n10/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"8.\n執行秘書應針對完整評估編製一份報告，且該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議中，提交予執行附屬機構審議，以期為該次締約方大會審議提供建議。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n執行秘書應針對完整評估編製一份報告，且該報告應於第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議中，提交予執行附屬機構審議，以期為該次締約方大會審議提供建議。</p>"},{"md":"9.\n在第十八次會議期間，將邀請締約方大會注意到全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期內，為執行本公約及其議定書所必需之資金估算金額。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n在第十八次會議期間，將邀請締約方大會注意到全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期內，為執行本公約及其議定書所必需之資金估算金額。</p>"},{"md":"附件 III\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍","html":"<p>附件 III<br />\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍</p>"},{"md":"A.\n目標","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標</p>"},{"md":"1.\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第二十一條第三項$^22$並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，本公約締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並視必要採取適當行動以提高財務機制的有效性。為此，審查應包含下列要素：\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動與締約方大會指引之符合性；\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面的有效性，以使符合條件的開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，能夠支付其透過執行措施以履行其在本公約及其議定書下之義務，且該等措施能產生全球環境效益並從其規定中獲益之所達成之議定全額增量成本，並考量資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面的效率，並根據締約方大會之指引，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；\n(d) 配合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與本公約及其議定書相關之事項），在催化與強化國家執行措施方面的有效性；\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於執行本公約、達成其三大目標以及（如適用）執行其議定書之活動的效率與有效性，並考量締約方大會所提供之指引；\n(f) 資源部署與使用之流程與程序的效率與有效性，包括簡化程序與取得模式；\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之執行產生綜效，且與各該協議之授權一致之方式下，為本公約及其議定書目標提供支持之有效性與效率；","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第二十一條第三項<sup>22</sup>並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，本公約締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並視必要採取適當行動以提高財務機制的有效性。為此，審查應包含下列要素：<br />\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動與締約方大會指引之符合性；<br />\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面的有效性，以使符合條件的開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，能夠支付其透過執行措施以履行其在本公約及其議定書下之義務，且該等措施能產生全球環境效益並從其規定中獲益之所達成之議定全額增量成本，並考量資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；<br />\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面的效率，並根據締約方大會之指引，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；<br />\n(d) 配合達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之國家優先事項（包括與本公約及其議定書相關之事項），在催化與強化國家執行措施方面的有效性；<br />\n(e) 由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於執行本公約、達成其三大目標以及（如適用）執行其議定書之活動的效率與有效性，並考量締約方大會所提供之指引；<br />\n(f) 資源部署與使用之流程與程序的效率與有效性，包括簡化程序與取得模式；<br />\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之執行產生綜效，且與各該協議之授權一致之方式下，為本公約及其議定書目標提供支持之有效性與效率；</p>"},{"md":"$^22$ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p><sup>22</sup> 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>"}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p011.md","en":"                                                                                   CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n             (h) The effectiveness in improving access to financial resources and trends associated with\n       funding for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth to support the\n       implementation of the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols;\n             (i)    The efficiency of each of the implementing agencies of the Global Environment Facility\n       in providing technical support and services to countries in their preparation of project proposals and\n       the implementation of projects, including with regard to the timely disbursement of fund, fees and\n       project management costs, use of international consultants and control of expenditure.\n       B.      Methodology\n       2.   The review will cover all the activities of the institutional structure operating the financial\n       mechanism, in particular for the period from 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2026.\n       3.    The review shall draw upon, inter alia, and in a balanced manner, the following sources of\n       information:\n             (a) The reviews of effectiveness of the financial mechanism in implementing the\n       Convention undertaken pursuant to the memorandum of understanding between the Conference of\n       the Parties to the Convention and the Council of the Global Environment Facility, as contained in the\n       annex to decision III/8 of 15 November 1996;\n              (b) Reports prepared by the Global Environment Facility, including its reports for meetings\n       of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention;\n              (c) Reports of the Independent Evaluation Office of the Global Environment Facility that\n       relate to the biodiversity-related activities of the Facility, including the eighth comprehensive\n       evaluation of the Global Environment Facility, as well as relevant assessments by the agencies\n       accredited by the Council of the Facility and other partners;\n              (d) The Multilateral Performance Network 23 assessments of the Global Environment\n       Facility and relevant reports related to the review of the vertical climate and environmental funds;\n             (e) Information regarding the financial mechanism provided by Parties through national\n       reports and other submissions, surveys and interviews;\n              (f)   Information provided by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and\n       relevant stakeholders related to projects funded through the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund\n       and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, including their views on possible impacts on their\n       rights, as applicable, as well as documented evidence and assessments of such impacts, including\n       gender-differentiated impacts;\n               (g)     Experience with, and lessons learned from, relevant international financial mechanisms;\n             (h) The report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth\n       meeting of the Conference of the Parties;\n              (i)   The stocktake review of the operations and performance of the Global Biodiversity\n       Framework Fund regarding its scale, speed and accessibility and the future arrangements requested\n       in decision 15/15 of 19 December 2022.\n       C.      Criteria\n       4.   The effectiveness and efficiency of the financial mechanism should be assessed taking into\n       account, inter alia:\n            (a) The actions taken by the Global Environment Facility in response to the guidance of the\n       Conference of the Parties and to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,24 including\n\n\n23 See www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html.\n24 Decision 15/4, annex.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                        11/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"(h) 改善取得財務資源之成效，以及與為支持履行《公約》及其議定書目標之資金，提供予原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年相關之趨勢；\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在提供技術支援與服務以協助各國編制計畫提案及執行計畫方面之效率，包括關於資金、費用及計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之管控。","html":"<p>(h) 改善取得財務資源之成效，以及與為支持履行《公約》及其議定書目標之資金，提供予原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年相關之趨勢；<br />\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在提供技術支援與服務以協助各國編制計畫提案及執行計畫方面之效率，包括關於資金、費用及計畫管理成本之及時撥付、國際顧問之使用以及支出之管控。</p>"},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>"},{"md":"方法論","html":"<p>方法論</p>"},{"md":"2.\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。\n3.\n本次審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：\n(a) 根據《公約》締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會之間之諒解備忘錄（如 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載）所進行之財務機制在履行《公約》成效之審查；\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為《公約》締約方大會會議所編製之報告；\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與該基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由該基金理事會認證之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；\n(d) 多邊績效網絡$^{23}$對全球環境基金之評估，以及與審查垂直氣候與環境基金相關之報告；\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括其對其權利可能造成影響之觀點（如適用），以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；\n(g) 相關國際財務機制之經驗與經驗教訓；\n(h) 全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所編製之報告；\n(i) 針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之規模、速度與可取得性，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排，進行之營運與績效盤點審查。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n本次審查將涵蓋執行財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是自 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。<br />\n3.<br />\n本次審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：<br />\n(a) 根據《公約》締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會之間之諒解備忘錄（如 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載）所進行之財務機制在履行《公約》成效之審查；<br />\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為《公約》締約方大會會議所編製之報告；<br />\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與該基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由該基金理事會認證之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；<br />\n(d) 多邊績效網絡<sup>23</sup>對全球環境基金之評估，以及與審查垂直氣候與環境基金相關之報告；<br />\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；<br />\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，與透過全球環境基金信託基金及全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關之資訊，包括其對其權利可能造成影響之觀點（如適用），以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；<br />\n(g) 相關國際財務機制之經驗與經驗教訓；<br />\n(h) 全球環境基金理事會為第十七次締約方大會所編製之報告；<br />\n(i) 針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之規模、速度與可取得性，以及 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排，進行之營運與績效盤點審查。</p>"},{"md":"C.","html":"<p>C.</p>"},{"md":"標準","html":"<p>標準</p>"},{"md":"4.\n財務機制之成效與效率之評估，應考慮除其他外：\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》$^{24}$所採取之行動，包括","html":"<p>4.<br />\n財務機制之成效與效率之評估，應考慮除其他外：<br />\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會指引及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》<sup>24</sup>所採取之行動，包括</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{23}$ 參見 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。\n$^{24}$ 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>23</sup> 參見 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。<br />\n<sup>24</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>"}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p012.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\n        through the decisions of the Global Environment Facility Council on relations with conventions and\n        international institutions;\n                (b) The extent to which [all] eligible Parties[, including developing countries, in particular\n        the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in\n        transition] take measures to apply for and receive timely, adequate and predictable funding to enable\n        them to meet the agreed full incremental cost to them of implementing measures through which they\n        fulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental\n        benefits;\n              (c) Information provided by Parties in relation to their performance in delivering projects,\n        such as constraints affecting those Parties, as well as women and youth, under the Global\n        Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, and on the\n        performance of implementing agencies;\n             (d) Percentage of eligible Parties that have received financial support from the financial\n        mechanism for implementing global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the\n        Convention and its Protocols;\n               (e) Percentage of biodiversity-relevant funding through the financial mechanism in support\n        of the achievement of global biodiversity goals and targets;\n               (f)   Trends in co-financing, in particular private and non-grant financing in the biodiversity\n        focal area enabled by the financial mechanism;\n              (g) Trends in financing global, regional and subregional biodiversity projects under the\n        financial mechanism;\n              (h) Trends in financing that take into consideration synergies among conventions for which\n        the Global Environment Facility has been designated to operate their financial mechanism on an\n        ongoing and interim basis;\n               (i)   Trends in financing targeted at biodiversity-related conventions and agreements taking\n        into consideration synergies among them;\n              (j)   Trends in time frames for project development and resource disbursement, including the\n        time between the project approval and the first disbursement;\n            (k) Trends in financing targeted at or led by indigenous peoples and local communities,\n        women and youth, including progress on modalities of access to finance;\n              (l)    Trends in the number and themes of capacity-building activities that enable Parties and\n        stakeholders to secure access to financing from the Global Environment Facility;\n               [(m) Trends in project financing leading to high sustainability or durability ratings and long-\n        term results achieved through biodiversity programming supported by the Global Environment\n        Facility in relation to expected results planned by the Facility through that programming;]\n              [(n)   Criteria listed in decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025.]\n        5.     The assessment should include a comparison of the Global Environment Facility with the\n        financial mechanisms of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including the Green\n        Climate Fund, the Adaptation Fund and the Fund for Responding to Loss and Damage. Elements for\n        consideration should include: contributor base; funding modalities and financial performance;\n        criteria and processes for funding, including project cycle considerations; access and disbursement\n        modalities (e.g. direct allocation or project-based disbursement), including for indigenous peoples\n        and local communities, women and youth; relationship between the governing body of the fund and\n        the Conference of the Parties to the respective multilateral environmental agreement; transparency,\n        monitoring, reporting and evaluation; accreditation process and role and performance of\n        implementing agencies; cost-effectiveness of operations; ability to leverage funding to mobilize\n\n12/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；\n(b) [所有] 合格締約方[，包括開發中國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方] 採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金，以使其能夠承擔因執行措施而產生的、符合其履行《公約》及其議定書義務並產生全球環境效益之約定全額增量成本之程度；\n(c) 締約方就其在全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下執行專案之績效所提供之資訊，例如影響該等締約方以及女性與青年的限制因素，以及執行機構之績效；\n(d) 合格締約方中，已從財務機制獲得財務支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之生物多樣性相關資金百分比；\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制所促成之生物多樣性重點領域內，私人及非撥款性質之融資趨勢；\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；\n(h) 考量各公約間綜效之融資趨勢，其中全球環境基金已被指定持續且臨時地負責運作該等公約之財務機制；\n(i) 考量各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效之針對性融資趨勢；\n(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括專案核准至首次撥付之間的時間；\n(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之融資趨勢，包括取得資金方式之進展；\n(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠確保取得全球環境基金資金之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；\n[(m) 專案融資趨勢，其導致高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫所規劃之預期結果之關係；]\n[(n)\n列於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中之標準。]","html":"<p>透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議；<br />\n(b) [所有] 合格締約方[，包括開發中國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方] 採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金，以使其能夠承擔因執行措施而產生的、符合其履行《公約》及其議定書義務並產生全球環境效益之約定全額增量成本之程度；<br />\n(c) 締約方就其在全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下執行專案之績效所提供之資訊，例如影響該等締約方以及女性與青年的限制因素，以及執行機構之績效；<br />\n(d) 合格締約方中，已從財務機制獲得財務支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；<br />\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標之生物多樣性相關資金百分比；<br />\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制所促成之生物多樣性重點領域內，私人及非撥款性質之融資趨勢；<br />\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；<br />\n(h) 考量各公約間綜效之融資趨勢，其中全球環境基金已被指定持續且臨時地負責運作該等公約之財務機制；<br />\n(i) 考量各生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效之針對性融資趨勢；<br />\n(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括專案核准至首次撥付之間的時間；<br />\n(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之融資趨勢，包括取得資金方式之進展；<br />\n(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠確保取得全球環境基金資金之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；<br />\n[(m) 專案融資趨勢，其導致高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫所規劃之預期結果之關係；]<br />\n[(n)<br />\n列於 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中之標準。]</p>"},{"md":"5.\n評估應包括全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金、適應基金以及損失與損害基金。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資金模式與財務績效；資金之標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付方式（例如直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之方式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；業務之成本效益；利用資金以動員……","html":"<p>5.<br />\n評估應包括全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金、適應基金以及損失與損害基金。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資金模式與財務績效；資金之標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付方式（例如直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之方式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監測、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；業務之成本效益；利用資金以動員……</p>"}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae1dae4205fddf16766486c/p013.md","en":"                                                                            CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13\n\nadditional finance for biodiversity; cost of setting up and running the financial instrument; leveraging\npublic and private co-finance; and integration of various environmental fields.\nD.    Procedures for implementation\n6.    In consultation with the Bureau, the Executive Secretary will contract an experienced\nindependent evaluator to undertake the review, in accordance with the aforementioned objectives,\nmethodology and criteria.\n7.    The evaluator will undertake desk studies, questionnaire surveys, interviews and field visits,\nsuch as may be required for the implementation of the review, and collaborate for that purpose with\nthe Global Environment Facility and its Independent Evaluation Office, as well as other independent\nassessments, such as those of the Multilateral Performance Network, if necessary, and prepare a\ncompilation and synthesis of the information received.\n8.     Special efforts should be made to collect the views of Parties, indigenous peoples and local\ncommunities, women and youth, including, as applicable, information on possible impacts on their\nrights, and of the private sector and non-governmental organizations, in relation to project-specific\nenvironmental objectives and in accordance with relevant national legislation.\n9.   The draft synthesis report and recommendations of the evaluator will be made available to the\nGlobal Environment Facility for its review and comments. Such comments will be included in the\ndocumentation and identified by source.\n10. The report should include as an annex the study requested in paragraph 41 of decision 16/33\nof 27 February 2025 [benchmarking the Global Environment Facility against the financial\nmechanisms or similar instruments of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements,\nincluding with regard to their legal nature, funding modalities and financial performance, criteria and\nprocess for funding, access and disbursement modalities, monitoring and evaluation, governance and\nthe cost-effectiveness of operations[, as well as other criteria contained in decision 16/34]].\n11.   The report shall include as an annex the stocktake review referred to in decision 15/15.\n12. On the basis of the synthesis report and recommendations of the independent evaluator, the\nExecutive Secretary will prepare, in consultation with the Council and the Secretariat of the Global\nEnvironment Facility, a draft decision on the seventh quadrennial review of the financial mechanism,\nincluding specific suggestions for action to improve the effectiveness of the mechanism, as\nnecessary, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation, with its recommendations\nto be submitted to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting.\n                                             __________\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                  13/13","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/CRP.13</p>"},{"md":"生物多樣性之追加財務；建立與運作財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。\nD.","html":"<p>生物多樣性之追加財務；建立與運作財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。<br />\nD.</p>"},{"md":"執行程序","html":"<p>執行程序</p>"},{"md":"6.\n執行秘書應與主席團協商，並聘請一位經驗豐富的獨立評估員，根據前述目標、方法論與準則進行審查。\n7.\n評估員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視執行審查之需求而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室進行合作，必要時亦應與其他獨立評估機構（例如多邊績效網絡）進行合作，並編纂與綜合所收到的資訊。\n8.\n應特別努力收集締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年（包括視適用情況，收集關於其權利可能受到的影響之資訊），以及私營部門與非政府組織對於特定專案環境目標之看法，並應符合相關國家立法。\n9.\n評估員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。此類評論應納入文件中，並標明來源。\n10. 報告應包含一項附件，即決議 16/33（2025 年 2 月 27 日）第 41 段所要求的研究[將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助模式與財務績效、資助準則與程序、取得與撥付模式、監測與評估、治理以及運作之成本效益[，以及決議 16/34 中包含的其他準則]]。\n11.\n報告應包含一項附件，即決議 15/15 中所提及的進度審查。\n12. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估員之綜合報告與建議，並與理事會及全球環境基金秘書處協商，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查的決議草案，包括必要時旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議，以供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。\n__________","html":"<p>6.<br />\n執行秘書應與主席團協商，並聘請一位經驗豐富的獨立評估員，根據前述目標、方法論與準則進行審查。<br />\n7.<br />\n評估員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視執行審查之需求而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室進行合作，必要時亦應與其他獨立評估機構（例如多邊績效網絡）進行合作，並編纂與綜合所收到的資訊。<br />\n8.<br />\n應特別努力收集締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年（包括視適用情況，收集關於其權利可能受到的影響之資訊），以及私營部門與非政府組織對於特定專案環境目標之看法，並應符合相關國家立法。<br />\n9.<br />\n評估員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。此類評論應納入文件中，並標明來源。<br />\n10. 報告應包含一項附件，即決議 16/33（2025 年 2 月 27 日）第 41 段所要求的研究[將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助模式與財務績效、資助準則與程序、取得與撥付模式、監測與評估、治理以及運作之成本效益[，以及決議 16/34 中包含的其他準則]]。<br />\n11.<br />\n報告應包含一項附件，即決議 15/15 中所提及的進度審查。<br />\n12. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估員之綜合報告與建議，並與理事會及全球環境基金秘書處協商，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查的決議草案，包括必要時旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議，以供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。</p>\n<hr />"},{"md":"13/13","html":"<p>13/13</p>"}]}]};
